IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pl-types`
IMPORT `pl-eligibility`

-- Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 — GOAL 2: LEAVE.
--
--   "May the employee take primary carer leave, partner's leave, extended
--    leave or special leave; for how long; from when; and may they request
--    negotiated carer leave?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1987_129.txt — Parts 1-3A,
-- ss 8-30J.

§ `Goal 2 — leave`

§§ `Primary carer leave (ss 8-14)`

-- s 6 bars all parental leave under this Act (s 2: primary carer leave,
-- partner's leave and extended leave).
@ref s 6
GIVEN c IS A `Parental leave case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6 bars parental leave in` c IF
    `s 6 bars leave, previous leave for another child ended` (c's `the leave history`'s `previous parental leave for another child ended on`) `, leave starting` (`the day the leave or payments start, for` (c's `the child concerned`))

-- s 8 "(1) An employee may take primary carer leave if the employee— (a) is
-- the primary carer in respect of a child; and (b) meets the 6-month
-- employment test or the 12-month employment test. (2) No employee may take
-- primary carer leave ... if the employee has previously taken a period of
-- leave in respect of that child ... (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to an
-- employee who is a primary carer under section 7(1)(b)(iii)." s 6 bars
-- leave within 6 months of leave for another child; it is checked at the
-- day the leave starts (FORK F4).
@ref ss 6, 8
GIVEN c IS A `Parental leave case`, t IS AN `Employment test`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may take primary carer leave, case` c `, test met` t IF
        `is the primary carer` (c's `the carer facts`)
    AND `meets an employment test` t
    AND (    NOT c's `the leave history`'s `previously took parental leave for this child`
         OR  `the primary carer kind of` (c's `the carer facts`) EQUALS `(b)(iii) the mother's spouse or partner who took permanent primary responsibility`)
    AND NOT `s 6 bars parental leave in` c

-- s 9(1) "Primary carer leave must be taken in 1 continuous period not
-- exceeding 26 weeks". (2) a female employee whose leave begins on a date in
-- a certificate (s 13) or appointed by her employer (s 14) "shall be
-- entitled to take at least 20 weeks of her primary carer leave after the
-- expected date of delivery and, if necessary for that purpose, to extend
-- the duration of her primary carer leave."
@ref s 9(1)-(2)
GIVEN start IS A DATE, edd IS A DATE, `certificate or employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most primary carer leave, in weeks, starting` start `, expected delivery` edd `, begun under s 13 or 14:` `certificate or employer` MEANS
    IF   `certificate or employer`
    THEN max 26 (((Day edd MINUS Day start) DIVIDED BY 7) PLUS 20)
    ELSE 26

-- s 11 "Primary carer leave may, at the option of the employee and subject
-- to compliance with section 37, begin on a date which is earlier, by not
-- more than 6 weeks than,— (a) in the case of a child to be born to the
-- employee, the expected date of delivery; or (b) in any other case, the
-- date on which the employee intends to become the primary carer".
@ref s 11
GIVEN from IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest start the employee may choose, from` from MEANS
    `the day` (0 MINUS 42) `days after` from

-- s 15(1) "A female employee who is pregnant is entitled, before taking
-- primary carer leave, to take a total of up to 10 days' special leave
-- without pay for reasons connected with her pregnancy."
@ref s 15
`the special leave without pay, in days` MEANS 10

§§ `Partner's leave (ss 17-22)`

-- s 17 "(1) An employee may take partner's leave if the employee— (a) is
-- the spouse or partner of the primary carer ...; and (b) assumes or
-- intends to assume responsibility for the care of that child; and (c)
-- meets the 6-month employment test or the 12-month employment test. (2)
-- ... may not take partner's leave ... if— (a) the employee has previously
-- taken ... partner's leave ...; or (b) the employee is the biological
-- mother of the child and transferred her parental leave payment
-- entitlements to her spouse or partner under section 71E."
@ref s 17
GIVEN c IS A `Parental leave case`, t IS AN `Employment test`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may take partner's leave, case` c `, test met` t IF
        c's `is the primary carer's spouse or partner and assumes care`
    AND `meets an employment test` t
    AND NOT c's `the leave history`'s `previously took partner's leave for this child`
    AND NOT `s 6 bars parental leave in` c
    AND NOT (    c's `the carer facts`'s `is the biological mother`
             AND c's `the leave history`'s `the mother transferred her payment entitlement under s 71E`)

-- s 19 "Partner's leave must be taken in 1 continuous period not
-- exceeding— (a) 2 weeks if the employee meets the 12-month employment
-- test; or (b) 1 week if the employee meets the 6-month employment test."
@ref s 19
GIVEN t IS AN `Employment test`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the partner's leave, in weeks, for` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `the 12-month employment test` THEN 2
    WHEN `the 6-month employment test`  THEN 1
    WHEN `neither employment test`      THEN 0

-- s 21 "(a) in the case of a child to be born to the employee's spouse or
-- partner, on any date in the period— (i) beginning on the 21st day before
-- the expected date of delivery; and (ii) ending with the close of the 21st
-- day after the actual date of delivery or, if the child is discharged from
-- a hospital ... more than 21 days after the actual date of delivery, the
-- close of the day on which the child is discharged ...; or (b) in any other
-- case, ... beginning on the 21st day before the date on which the
-- employee's spouse or partner intends to become the primary carer ... and
-- ... ending with the close of the 21st day after the actual date". s 22:
-- any date by agreement.
@ref s 21
GIVEN c IS A Child, discharged IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day partner's leave may begin at the employee's option, for` c `, discharged` discharged MEANS
    IF   c's `born to the person or their spouse or partner`
    THEN `the day` (0 MINUS 21) `days after` (c's `expected date of delivery`)
    ELSE `the day` (0 MINUS 21) `days after` (c's `first date the person or their spouse or partner becomes the primary carer`)

@ref s 21
GIVEN c IS A Child, discharged IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day partner's leave may begin at the employee's option, for` c `, discharged` discharged MEANS
    IF   c's `born to the person or their spouse or partner`
    THEN CONSIDER c's `date of birth`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `the child is not yet born, so the s 21(a)(ii) date is not yet fixed`
         WHEN JUST b THEN
            CONSIDER discharged
            WHEN JUST h THEN IF h GREATER THAN `the day` 21 `days after` b THEN h ELSE `the day` 21 `days after` b
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day` 21 `days after` b
    ELSE `the day` 21 `days after` (c's `first date the person or their spouse or partner becomes the primary carer`)

`the child is not yet born, so the s 21(a)(ii) date is not yet fixed` MEANS
    REFUSE "the child is not yet born, so the s 21(a)(ii) date is not yet fixed"

§§ `Extended leave (ss 23-29)`

-- s 26(1) "the maximum amount of extended leave that an individual employee
-- may take in respect of a child is— (a) 26 weeks, if the employee meets the
-- 6-month employment test; or (b) 52 weeks, if the employee meets the
-- 12-month employment test."
@ref ss 23(1)(b), 26(1)
GIVEN t IS AN `Employment test`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the individual extended leave, in weeks, for` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `the 12-month employment test` THEN 52
    WHEN `the 6-month employment test`  THEN 26
    WHEN `neither employment test`      THEN 0

-- s 26(2) "If an employee and that employee's spouse or partner are each
-- individually entitled to extended leave in respect of the same child, the
-- maximum combined entitlement ... is— (a) 26 weeks, if both meet the
-- 6-month employment test; or (b) 52 weeks, if both meet the 12-month
-- employment test; or (c) 52 weeks, if one meets the 12-month employment test
-- and the other meets the 6-month employment test (in which case the person
-- who meets the 6-month employment test may not take more than 26 weeks
-- ...)." Where the spouse or partner is not entitled, s 26(1) alone applies.
@ref s 26(1)-(2)
GIVEN own IS AN `Employment test`, partner IS AN `Employment test`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the extended leave pool, in weeks, own test` own `, partner's test` partner MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `meets an employment test` partner THEN `the individual extended leave, in weeks, for` own
        IF NOT `meets an employment test` own     THEN `the individual extended leave, in weeks, for` partner
        IF own EQUALS `the 6-month employment test` AND partner EQUALS `the 6-month employment test` THEN 26
        OTHERWISE 52

-- s 26(3) "If an employee takes primary carer leave ..., the period of
-- extended leave to which the employee and his or her spouse or partner are
-- entitled ... is the relevant period specified in subsection (1) or (2)
-- reduced by the total period of primary carer leave taken, excluding any
-- period of primary carer leave in excess of 26 weeks taken under section
-- 9(2)." s 28(1) "(a) neither ... takes ... extended leave that ... exceed[s]
-- the amount ... to which that person is individually entitled under section
-- 26(1); and (b) the total ... does not exceed the maximum combined period".
-- FORK F1: the person's own s 26(1) amount is reduced by the person's own
-- primary carer leave; the shared pool by both people's. So a 6-month
-- employee who takes 26 weeks of primary carer leave has no extended leave
-- left, as s 1B(3)(a) describes.
@ref ss 23, 26, 28
@export The extended leave the employee may still take under ss 23, 26 and 28 of the Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 (NZ): the lesser of their own maximum (26 weeks on the 6-month test, 52 on the 12-month test, less their own primary carer leave and extended leave) and what is left of the pool shared with their spouse or partner (26 or 52 weeks, less both people's primary carer leave up to 26 weeks and extended leave). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN own IS AN `Employment test`  @desc The employment test the employee meets
      partner IS AN `Employment test`  @desc The employment test the spouse or partner meets (neither, if they are not entitled to extended leave)
      h IS A `Leave history`  @desc Primary carer leave and extended leave already taken by each of them
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the extended leave remaining, in weeks, own test` own `, partner's test` partner `, history` h MEANS
    IF   `meets an employment test` own
    THEN max 0 (min ownLeft poolLeft)
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        ownPcl     MEANS min 26 (h's `primary carer leave taken by the person, in weeks`)
        spousePcl MEANS min 26 (h's `primary carer leave taken by the spouse or partner, in weeks`)
        ownLeft    MEANS (`the individual extended leave, in weeks, for` own) MINUS (ownPcl PLUS h's `extended leave already taken by the person, in weeks`)
        poolLeft   MEANS (`the extended leave pool, in weeks, own test` own `, partner's test` partner)
                         MINUS (ownPcl PLUS spousePcl
                                PLUS h's `extended leave already taken by the person, in weeks`
                                PLUS h's `extended leave already taken by the spouse or partner, in weeks`)

-- s 27(3) "applicable end date means,— (a) if the employee, or the
-- employee's spouse or partner, qualifies for extended leave under section
-- 23(1)(b)(i) (... the 6-month employment test),— (i) in the case of a child
-- born to the employee, or to the employee's spouse or partner, the date on
-- which the child attains the age of 6 months; or (ii) in any other case,
-- the date that is 6 months after the first date on which either ...
-- becomes the primary carer ...; or (b) if ... under section 23(1)(b)(ii)
-- (... the 12-month employment test),— (i) ... the age of 12 months; or (ii)
-- ... the first anniversary". (4) "No employee is entitled to start or
-- continue any period of extended leave under this Act after— (a) the
-- applicable end date". FORK F2: where one of them meets the 12-month test,
-- (b) applies.
@ref s 27(3)-(4)
GIVEN c IS A Child, own IS AN `Employment test`, partner IS AN `Employment test`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of extended leave for` c `, own test` own `, partner's test` partner MEANS
    `add months` from months
    WHERE
        months MEANS
            IF own EQUALS `the 12-month employment test` OR partner EQUALS `the 12-month employment test` THEN 12 ELSE 6
        from MEANS
            IF   c's `born to the person or their spouse or partner`
            THEN CONSIDER c's `date of birth`
                 WHEN JUST b THEN b
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN `the child is not yet born, so the s 27(3) end date is not yet fixed`
            ELSE c's `first date the person or their spouse or partner becomes the primary carer`

`the child is not yet born, so the s 27(3) end date is not yet fixed` MEANS
    REFUSE "the child is not yet born, so the s 27(3) end date is not yet fixed"

§§ `Negotiated carer leave (Part 3A)`

-- s 30B(1) "This section applies to an employee who— (a) is not entitled
-- to primary carer leave; but (b) is entitled to parental leave payments
-- under section 71D(1) if the employee takes leave".
@ref s 30B(1)
GIVEN `entitled to primary carer leave` IS A BOOLEAN, `entitled to payments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may request negotiated carer leave, entitled to primary carer leave:` `entitled to primary carer leave` `, to payments if on leave:` `entitled to payments` IF
    (NOT `entitled to primary carer leave`) AND `entitled to payments`

-- s 30B(3) "(a) ... at least 3 months before the expected date of delivery;
-- or (b) ... a primary carer under section 7(1)(b)(iii), within a reasonable
-- period after ...; or (c) in any other case, at least 14 days prior to the
-- date on which the employee intends to become the primary carer". The
-- same deadlines apply to notice of parental leave (ss 31(3)(a), 33(b)).
-- FORK F3: "at least 14 days" before an event leaves 14 clear days (the
-- Legislation Act 2019's rule for "at least" a number of days between 2
-- events); "at least 3 months before" is met on the day 3 months before.
@ref ss 30B(3), 31(3), 33
GIVEN c IS A Child
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to request or give notice, for` c MEANS
    IF   c's `born to the person or their spouse or partner`
    THEN `add months` (c's `expected date of delivery`) (0 MINUS 3)
    ELSE `the day` (0 MINUS 15) `days after` (c's `first date the person or their spouse or partner becomes the primary carer`)

-- s 30D "An employer must deal with a request ... as soon as possible, but
-- not later than 1 month after receiving it".
@ref s 30D
GIVEN received IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the employer's decision, request received` received MEANS
    `add months` received 1

-- s 30E(2) "The grounds are— (a) inability to reorganise work among
-- existing staff: (b) inability to recruit additional staff: (c)
-- detrimental impact on quality: (d) detrimental impact on performance: (e)
-- planned structural changes: (f) burden of additional costs: (g)
-- detrimental effect on ability to meet customer demand." Anything else is
-- not a ground (s 30E(1) "only if").
@ref s 30E
GIVEN `grounds relied on` IS A NUMBER, `of which in s 30E(2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refusal rests on s 30E(2) grounds only, grounds relied on` `grounds relied on` `, of which in s 30E(2)` `of which in s 30E(2)` IF
        `grounds relied on` AT LEAST 1
    AND `of which in s 30E(2)` EQUALS `grounds relied on`

-- s 30I(3)-(4) "An application must be made within 12 months after the
-- relevant date. ... relevant date means,— (a) if the employer notifies a
-- refusal within 1 month after receiving a request, the date of the
-- notification: (b) in any other case, the date that is 1 month after the
-- employer received the employee's request."
@ref s 30I(3)-(4)
GIVEN received IS A DATE, refused IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply to the Authority under s 30I, request received` received `, refusal notified` refused MEANS
    `add years` relevant 1
    WHERE
        relevant MEANS
            CONSIDER refused
            WHEN JUST r THEN IF r AT MOST `add months` received 1 THEN r ELSE `add months` received 1
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `add months` received 1

-- s 30J(1) "An employer who does not comply with section 30D is liable to a
-- penalty not exceeding $2,000". (2) "payable to the employee concerned".
@ref s 30J
`the maximum penalty under s 30J` MEANS 2000
